# Home Lab Telegram bot — permitted user IDs, one per line.
#
# Installed to /etc/homelab-telegram-bot/allowlist
#
# These are numeric TELEGRAM USER IDs, not usernames. A username can be changed
# by its owner; the numeric id cannot, which is why the allowlist uses it.
#
# Find yours by messaging @userinfobot on Telegram, or by starting this bot,
# sending it any message, and reading the journal:
#
#     journalctl -u homelab-telegram-bot -n 20
#     refused: user 123456789 is not allowlisted
#
# This file is NOT a secret -- it holds numeric ids, nothing more -- but it is
# deployment-specific, so it lives on the node rather than in the repository.
#
# An EMPTY file is a hard error and the bot refuses to start. That is
# deliberate: the failure mode of a misconfigured allowlist must never be
# "answer everyone".

# 123456789
